"""English presentation only. Never alter raw records or original evidence bytes."""
import pathlib,json,re,html,zipfile,hashlib,sys
H=html.escape
CJK=re.compile(r'[\u3400-\u4dbf\u4e00-\u9fff\uf900-\ufaff]')
STYLE='<style>body{font:16px/1.55 system-ui;max-width:1200px;margin:32px auto;padding:0 20px;color:#17202a}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{border:1px solid #bbc;padding:9px;text-align:left}td img{width:260px}img{max-width:100%}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:#f1f4f7;padding:16px}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}a{color:#165eaf}</style>'
def doc(title,body):return '<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>'+H(title)+'</title>'+STYLE+body+'</html>'
def build(target):
 target=pathlib.Path(target)
 raw=target/'raw-midscene-omarchy-13930-real-gallery-no-model.html'; original=raw.read_bytes();s=original.decode()
 dump=json.loads(list(re.finditer(r'<script type="midscene_web_dump" data-group-id="[^"]+"[^>]*>(.*?)</script>',s,re.S))[-1][1]);assert not CJK.search(json.dumps(dump,ensure_ascii=False))
 executions={x['name'].removeprefix('Log - '):x for x in dump['executions']};steps=json.loads((target/'raw-steps.json').read_text());assert len(steps)==len(executions)==37
 images={m[1]:m[2].strip() for m in re.finditer(r'<script type="midscene-image" data-id="([^"]+)">\s*(data:image/png;base64,[^<]+)</script>',s)}
 rows=[];native=[]
 for step in steps:
  name=step['id'];e=executions[name];uid=e['id'];task=e['tasks'][0];ref=task['recorder'][0]['screenshot']['id'];pic='raw-'+step['screenshot'].replace('/','-');href='midscene-english.html#'+uid
  info=f'<p>Recorded step: <code>{H(name)}</code><br>Original Midscene execution ID: <code>{uid}</code><br>Task ID: <code>{task["taskId"]}</code><br>Screenshot reference: <code>{ref}</code></p>'
  body=f'<h1>{H(name)}</h1>{info}<p><a href="{href}">English Midscene presentation: this execution</a> · <a href="index.html">Acceptance report</a></p><p>The observer record and screenshots are unchanged. This evidence page is an English presentation, not a new execution.</p><img src="{pic}" alt="{H(name)}"><pre>{H(json.dumps(step,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))}</pre>'
  (target/f'evidence-{uid}.html').write_text(doc(name,body))
  rows.append(f'<tr><td>{H(name)}</td><td><a href="{pic}"><img loading="lazy" src="{pic}" alt="{H(name)}"></a></td><td><code>{H(step["observed"]["value"])}</code><br>Popup open: {str(step["observed"]["popup"]).lower()}<br>Automated assertion passed; independent image review agrees.</td><td><a href="evidence-{uid}.html">Evidence page</a><br><a href="{href}">Midscene execution</a><br><code>{uid}</code></td></tr>')
  native.append(f'<section id="{uid}"><h2>{H(name)}</h2>{info}<img loading="lazy" src="{images[ref]}" alt="Original Midscene screenshot for {H(name)}"><details><summary>Unchanged execution record</summary><pre>{H(json.dumps(e,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))}</pre></details></section>')
 intro='<h1>English presentation of the original Midscene evidence</h1><p>This is a derived, English-only viewer of the 37 unchanged execution records and original inline PNG images. It is not the original Midscene application, a translated execution, or a product rerun. Original UUIDs are used as section IDs. No model calls were made.</p><p><a href="index.html">Acceptance report</a> · <a download href="original-evidence.tar.gz">Download immutable original evidence archive</a></p><p>The original Midscene HTML is retained byte-for-byte in that archive and at its original published path. Its bundled application resources contain non-English strings; the viewer below does not load those resources.</p>'
 (target/'midscene-english.html').write_text(doc('English Midscene evidence viewer',intro+''.join(native)))
 pins=json.loads((target/'raw-versions-source-pins.json').read_text())
 body='''<h1>Omarchy #13930: real desktop acceptance</h1><p><strong>Passed within the stated runtime and input-device scope.</strong> The fifth complete acceptance run passed. Independent review checked 37 recorded steps, 110 original file hashes, actual horizontal input events, and restoration/cleanup metadata. This is the real shared-component gallery, not business-panel end-to-end coverage.</p><p>This English presentation supersedes the original report's Chinese presentation. Evidence, screenshots, execution IDs, results and limitations are unchanged. No product rerun was performed. At publication preparation, PR #13930 remained open and unmerged with head <code>8997958d8e6419e384e68057fb37fe09a148e697</code>; the production diff contained only 32 added lines in <code>shell/Ui/Dropdown.qml</code>. No upstream comment was posted by this publication task.</p>
<h2>Results and limitations</h2><ul><li>On the candidate, closed downward wheel input selects clock → weather → power; upward input reverses that sequence. Both ends clamp without wrapping. The baseline keeps the selection unchanged and allows the surrounding page to scroll.</li><li>The gallery's actual initial value <code>Clock</code> matches no option. One downward notch selects the first option, <code>omarchy.clock</code>, on the candidate; the baseline remains <code>Clock</code>. The first upward notch from an unmatched value was not tested.</li><li>Wheeling over the trigger while the popup is open preserves the selected clock value and keeps the popup open on both revisions. Escape closes it. Keyboard input selects weather and returns to clock. The mouse regression test clicks the already-selected first option and closes the popup; it does not test selection of a different option.</li><li>Four horizontal injections used a temporary standard Linux uinput mouse: left/right on both baseline and candidate. Guest evdev records show EV_REL code 6 (REL_HWHEEL), -1/+1, with no code 8 (REL_WHEEL) contamination. Neither revision changes selection. In contrast, QMP's named wheel-left emitted code 8 = -2 in this configuration and is retained only as a diagnostic, not horizontal proof.</li><li>Fine-grained touchpad/sub-notch accumulation, physical devices, other desktop scale settings, the unmatched upward first notch, cross-option mouse selection and business-panel E2E are not covered. The actual desktop was 1280×800 at scale 1; scale 1.5 was only a coordinate unit check.</li><li>Input was deterministic QMP/uinput. Midscene recorded the real screen without model calls. Read-only gallery instrumentation observed state, focus and geometry. Exact baseline/head component bytes were compared; no product fix or stub was introduced to make the run pass.</li></ul>
<h2>Runtime and restoration</h2><p>The newer Qt 6.12 / Quickshell 0.3.2-6 image exposed a separate Color name-resolution compatibility problem, associated with upstream issue #15069. This successful comparison used Qt 6.11.2 / Quickshell 0.3.1 packages from the official Arch 2026/10/01 archive. Package hashes, signature-install logs and environment metadata are retained. These results do not establish that the Qt 6.12 problem is fixed.</p><p>The original and restored Dropdown and Gallery hashes match. Both files' original owner/group 0:0 and mode 644 were restored. The temporary input socket was removed and the test input device was absent after cleanup. The VM was disposable; this is not a claim that all operating-system packages were rolled back.</p>
<p><a href="raw-guest-original-hashes.json">Original hashes</a> · <a href="raw-guest-restored-hashes.json">Restored hashes</a> · <a href="raw-versions-original-permissions.txt">Original permissions</a> · <a href="raw-versions-restored-permissions.txt">Restored permissions</a> · <a href="raw-guest-input-cleanup.json">Input cleanup</a> · <a href="independent-review.json">Independent review and native ID mapping</a></p>
<h2>Reproducibility and immutable evidence</h2><p>Baseline: <code>8b4eae66da2938ba9559f103b18dbf85cdf28a70</code>. Acceptance harness: <code>978b6fa9365ee8603103c45545dfcbb745c7692a</code>. Complete acceptance run: 38748420827, job 116468073940. Fixed delivery commit: <code>3c4dfe405ffbd911a64a78d57e8d73d0f3c3faf8</code>.</p><p><a href="midscene-english.html">English Midscene presentation</a> · <a download href="original-evidence.tar.gz">Immutable original archive</a>. The archive is 10,693,573 bytes, SHA256 <code>b9317f0f708fb3ba31c90b04c72b0da1ce133f4f7eff9005bb4f0ce0644b683e</code>. Eight recovery chunks and all 110 internal SHA256 entries were verified. The original completion metadata says independent review was pending at generation time; the subsequent review is recorded separately without modifying the original.</p>'''
 body+='<pre>'+H(json.dumps(pins,indent=2))+'</pre><h2>Retained failure history</h2><ul>'
 for run,note in [('38706746908','Prerequisite check only; not complete acceptance.'),('38707818900','Failed: Qt 6.12 Color resolution and an early window-coordinate error. Original archive SHA256: 34242e19e1895ee975310e9e1a8993c11f3e37743a4263b0d86eb02006f48621.'),('38718038618','Intentional diagnostic failure confirming QQuickColor versus qs.Commons.Color resolution.'),('38721940032','Failed: core steps completed, but QMP wheel-left was actually vertical. Original archive SHA256: 5d006bd3edb24b373a9915334a62c0e0c687e51236db9fc382a2d3293fd2d85d.'),('38732887007','Failed: ScrollView moved the target offscreen to y824; bounds checking rejected it. Original archive SHA256: c6b55eed6eafe4bd8769f97767108aa093f269303fd8b105a508f899074819b9.'),('38748420827','Fifth complete acceptance run passed; sole basis for the passing result.'),('38766285794','Read-only recovery of original evidence; no product rerun.')]:body+=f'<li><a href="https://github.com/quanru/doubao-say/actions/runs/{run}">{run}</a>: {note}</li>'
 body+='</ul><p>Earlier failures remain in their original CI logs and recovered files; they are not combined into a passing run. This archive contains the fifth run, not every historical archive. Earlier Library references: libfile_22061a0446e48191943e56d4eb61c3ff (first archive), libfile_15570612f05c8191881f569f8a173444 (first log).</p><h2>English comment draft</h2><pre>'+H(pathlib.Path('acceptance/omarchy-13930/publish/comment.md').read_text())+'</pre><h2>Step-by-step evidence</h2><p>Every image is an unchanged original screenshot. Evidence pages retain the real Midscene execution UUIDs; the English viewer provides matching execution sections. No native-report deep links were invented.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Recorded step</th><th>Original screenshot</th><th>Observed result</th><th>Evidence / Midscene</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join(rows)+'</tbody></table>'
 (target/'index.html').write_text(doc('Omarchy 13930 acceptance report',body))
 assert raw.read_bytes()==original
 presentations=[target/'index.html',target/'midscene-english.html',*target.glob('evidence-*.html')];assert len(presentations)==39
 for f in presentations:assert not CJK.search(f.read_text()),f
 print(json.dumps({'english_html_pages':len(presentations),'unchanged_execution_records':len(executions),'original_midscene_sha256':sha(original)}))
def sha(b):return hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()
if __name__=='__main__':build(sys.argv[1])
